pposed to help me do something else and at seven so i texted him at 6 40 and now i called him and i was like hey where are you and he's like oh um unfortunately i won't be able to come i'm like your tone is different okay you don't answer the phone that way you always hey baby how are you you know you're not and then you're just not coming somewhere but you're expected to be and you don't feel like you have to be accountable okay to me um how did his actions at this point make you feel it made me feel like you forgot about me okay like i felt like we were on a good track i felt like we were doing everything right and then all of a sudden the only thing that changed was this friend of his who's you know came and now he can't call me he doesn't feel like he has to be accountable to me and it's not fair so i feel hurt i feel like betrayed almost and in your in your eyes how the feeling of betrayal like would spark that do you feel like it's more so of the other factor as far as the woman the the new person that's in his life business partner or do you feel like it's more of his actions that's making you feel the betrayal like what sparked it's definitely his actions like and i think the i assume it's because of her because she's the only thing that has changed okay his workload is still the same and the only difference is now she's here to help with all the business stuff um but i feel like up until that point he was always like not accountable but he like we owe each other something i deserve a phone call he acknowledged that i deserve a phone call if he's not going to be somewhere he would tell me he's a timely person he's dependable and the fact that he just didn't even think to say hey i know you expect me to be here but i'm not going to be there that hurts and at that moment when he said that he couldn't be there for what you needed him to be there for do you think that like based on um like what he said did that prompt you to lead to any other actions or feel any